\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Shared notation.}Standard number systems are $\mathbb N,\mathbb Z,\mathbb Q,\mathbb R,\mathbb C$. Specialized notation and index ranges follow the cited source and the definitions below.


The Karchmer-Raz-Wigderson composition conjecture concerns formula complexity of composed Boolean functions and its associated communication relation. Superpolynomial formula size exceeds $n^c$ for every fixed $c$ eventually.
\paragraph{Record scope and qualifications.}
The catalogue title is retained as metadata. Named certificates, contracts, bounds or frameworks in that title are not asserted as results of the original source extract.
The exact conjectural inequality is not printed in this supplied question; no circuit version or unrestricted direct-sum principle is substituted.

Source-record limitation: Duplicate full Karchmer-Raz-Wigderson composition target, retained in the more explicit supplied formulation under OWR ID 30004010; original DOI10.1007/BF01206317 and the primary 2017 composition paper identify the same conjecture.

Related catalogue records: \href{https://mehmetmars7.github.io/Erdosproblems-llm-hunter/problem.html?type=open_problems&id=30004010}{30004010}. Separate source IDs are preserved for their provenance.
\paragraph{Statement recorded in the supplied source.}
Can the Karchmer–Raz–Wigderson conjecture be proved in full generality, thereby implying superpolynomial formula-size lower bounds? \href{https://doi.org/10.4171/owr/2015/54}{[S2]}
\paragraph{Source status.}
The supplied catalogue labels this source record partially solved; that metadata was checked against the supplied snapshot on 2026-10-11. The label is preserved for provenance and is not an independent verification of present open status or mathematical correctness. The catalogue literature assessment is dated 2026-08-21.

\subsection{Short English statement}
Prove the stated composition lower-bound conjecture in full generality.

